</table>

<p>For most EPUB readers, the standard <strong>Palma 2 is the sweet spot</strong>: large enough for comfortable full-page reading, small enough to forget you are carrying it, and priced well below the color Pro model. If your EPUB library is mostly text — novels, nonfiction, textbooks — the B&amp;W screen is sharper and the battery lasts longer. Color matters most if you read graphic novels, illustrated books, or want stylus note-taking.</p>

<p>And if you want the smallest possible device, the Picco is worth a look — but the 3.97-inch screen is best for quick reading sessions, not long chapters.</p>

<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<section class="faq" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
