        <p>Yes. Because the Palma runs Android with the Google Play Store, you can install the Kindle, Kobo, or PocketBook apps and read books purchased from those stores. For EPUB files you own, however, native readers like NeoReader or KOReader usually give a better E Ink experience than the phone-oriented store apps.</p>
